      "widgets_values": [
        "LLM chat/completion with OpenCV 5's native LLM support - no Python ML framework, just cv2.dnn's new graph engine (KV-cache: the net's present.* outputs are routed back into its past_key_values.* inputs) + its built-in BPE/SentencePiece tokenizer.\n\n'CV LLM Generate' is ONE generic node: model folder, chat template and decode mode are dropdowns, so the same node covers Qwen2.5 / Gemma3 / GPT-2 family ONNX exports (e.g. optimum-cli export onnx --task causal-lm-with-past, or a merged transformers.js decoder - the node feeds the merged export's use_cache_branch for you). The two nodes below run the SAME model with and without a chat template: 'chatml (Qwen2.5)' wraps the prompt in the instruct format and gets an answer, 'none (raw prompt)' feeds it verbatim and gets a continuation.\n\nPick a model FOLDER, not a file: models/llm/opencv/qwen2.5-0.5b-instruct. The node finds the .onnx and the tokenizer inside it - the folder holds an OpenCV-format config.json + the family's tokenizer.json (from opencv_extra/testdata/dnn/llm/). The advanced 'lm_file' / 'tokenizer' dropdowns override that for unusual layouts. Every path is relative to the model root, so this workflow is portable - nothing points at one machine's disk.\n\nCPU decoding: a 0.5B fp32 model gives a few tokens/second - keep max_new_tokens small.\n\nAs of time of writing (01/08/2026) NOT EVERY MODEL RUNS (e.g. failed to run gpt-2)"
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
